From 2899e3f629a320f25020f2c93cf0a10039e4d071 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:48:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: bound the GMU's wait for a fault devcoredump

When a GMU OOB request or HFI message times out, a6xx_gmu_set_oob() and
a6xx_hfi_wait_for_msg_interrupt() wait for fault_coredump_done, in case
an SMMU fault's devcoredump has stalled the GPU, and retry. They wait with
no timeout. The fault handler marks the completion pending before
msm_gpu_fault_crashstate_capture() takes gpu->lock, and recover_worker()
holds gpu->lock across its GMU calls. When a GMU timeout in recovery meets
a pagefault, each side waits for the other for good: on the AYN Odin 2
Portal (A740) the gpu-worker sat in a6xx_gmu_set_oob(), the SMMU context
fault thread in msm_gpu_fault_crashstate_capture(), and the display stayed
frozen until a reboot. (This was raised when the wait was added; see
"drm/msm: Wait for MMU devcoredump when waiting for GMU".)

Wait at most 2 s, then report the timeout, so recovery goes on and the
devcoredump runs once gpu->lock is free.

y700 patch file: 0621-drm-msm-a6xx-bound-the-gmu-wait-for-a-fault-devcoredump.patch
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c | 8 ++++++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c | 8 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index f5168eb21..aa712627e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -443,9 +443,13 @@ int a6xx_gmu_set_oob(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu, enum a6xx_gmu_oob_state state)
 
 		/* We may timeout because the GMU is temporarily wedged from
 		 * pending faults from the GPU and we are taking a devcoredump.
-		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again.
+		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again, but not for
+		 * ever: the devcoredump takes gpu->lock, which our caller may
+		 * hold (recover_worker), and both would wait on each other.
 		 */
-		wait_for_completion(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done);
+		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done,
+						 msecs_to_jiffies(2000)))
+			break;
 	} while (true);
 
 	if (ret)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
index 186a73c0b..2c07b3b0f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
@@ -127,9 +127,13 @@ static int a6xx_hfi_wait_for_msg_interrupt(struct a6xx_gmu *gmu, u32 id, u32 seq
 
 		/* We may timeout because the GMU is temporarily wedged from
 		 * pending faults from the GPU and we are taking a devcoredump.
-		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again.
+		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again, but not for
+		 * ever: the devcoredump takes gpu->lock, which our caller may
+		 * hold (recover_worker), and both would wait on each other.
 		 */
-		wait_for_completion(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done);
+		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done,
+						 msecs_to_jiffies(2000)))
+			break;
 	} while (true);
 
 	if (ret) {
-- 
2.53.0

